<title>USA: Hightec settles suit.</title>
<headline>Hightec settles suit.</headline>
<dateline>SAN FRANCISCO 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hightec Inc on Tuesday said it settled a lawsuit with Benefits Administration Inc, a provider of private label benefits, resulting in a payment of $23,000 and promissory note for $227,000 to Hightec.</p>
<p>The settlement also includes a return of all stock issued by Hightec to Benefits Administration shareholders, Hightec said in a statement. It sued Benefits Administration in February to rescind an agreement between the two companies.</p>
<p>Hightec is a holding company with three operating subsidiaries The IPO Network, Sinclare Group Inc, and Karate International Corp.</p>
</text>
